      "body": "<!-- sdk-release-note-exempt: This release PR applies previously reviewed SDK changes and only updates release metadata and generated documentation. -->\n\nA stable release: npm moves `latest` to these versions.\n\n## What gets released\n\n| Package | Version | Bump | Changesets |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `@composio/core` | 0.28.0 → **0.29.0** | minor | `composio-client-update`, `custom-toolkit-mcp-url`, `local-tools-rename`, `sdk-rate-limit-handling` |\n| Python SDK (`composio` and every provider) | 0.31.0 → **0.32.0** | minor | `python-client-2-1-0`, `python-local-tools-rename`, `python-missing-api-key-message`, `python-rate-limit-handling` |\n| `@composio/slim` | 0.28.0 → **0.29.0** | minor | `custom-toolkit-mcp-url`, `local-tools-rename` |\n\n## Changesets consumed\n\n- `.changeset/composio-client-update.md` (`@composio/core` patch): Update @composio/client to 2.1.0 to include the latest API changes.\n- `.changeset/custom-toolkit-mcp-url.md` (`@composio/core` minor, `@composio/slim` minor): Breaking \\(experimental API\\): \\`composio.experimental.customToolkits.create\\(\\)\\` and \\`upsert\\(\\)\\` take the MCP server URL as \\`mcpUrl\\` instead of \\`appUrl\\`, and send it to the API as \\`mcp\\_url\\`.\n- `.changeset/local-tools-rename.md` (`@composio/core` minor, `@composio/slim` minor): Renames in-process custom tools to local tools, so they are no longer confused with the server-side custom toolkits on \\`composio.experimental.customToolkits\\`. Pass \\`experimental.localTools\\` and \\`expe…\n- `.changeset/python-client-2-1-0.md` (Python SDK (`composio` and every provider) minor): Update \\`composio-client\\` to 2.1.0. Breaking \\(experimental API\\): \\`composio.experimental.custom\\_toolkits.create\\(\\)\\` and \\`upsert\\(\\)\\` take the MCP server URL as \\`mcp\\_url\\` instead of \\`app\\_url\\`.\n- `.changeset/python-local-tools-rename.md` (Python SDK (`composio` and every provider) minor): Renames in-process custom tools to local tools, so they are no longer confused with the server-side custom toolkits on \\`composio.experimental.custom\\_toolkits\\`. Pass \\`experimental={\"local\\_tools\": ...,…\n- `.changeset/python-missing-api-key-message.md` (Python SDK (`composio` and every provider) patch): The error for a missing API key now explains how to set \\`COMPOSIO\\_API\\_KEY\\` or pass \\`api\\_key=\\`, and links to where to get a project API key, instead of suggesting \\`composio login\\`, which the Python pa…\n- `.changeset/python-rate-limit-handling.md` (Python SDK (`composio` and every provider) minor): \\`wait\\_for\\_connection\\(\\)\\` handles rate limits: the delay between polls grows from 1 to 5 seconds, and a poll rejected with a 429 waits as long as its \\`Retry-After\\` header asks \\(up to the timeout\\) and p…\n- `.changeset/sdk-rate-limit-handling.md` (`@composio/core` minor): Handle rate limits better: \\`tools.execute\\(\\)\\` reuses tool schemas instead of fetching one per call, \\`waitForConnection\\(\\)\\` backs off between polls and waits out a 429, and tool fetches and executions r…\n\n## Changelog and docs edits\n\n- Docs changelog entry: [`docs/content/changelog/11-09-26-sdk-42589989280.mdx`](https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/blob/sdk-release/batch-42589989280/docs/content/changelog/11-09-26-sdk-42589989280.mdx).\n- Package changelogs: [`python/CHANGELOG.md`](https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/blob/sdk-release/batch-42589989280/python/CHANGELOG.md), [`ts/packages/core/CHANGELOG.md`](https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/blob/sdk-release/batch-42589989280/ts/packages/core/CHANGELOG.md), [`ts/packages/slim/CHANGELOG.md`](https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/blob/sdk-release/batch-42589989280/ts/packages/slim/CHANGELOG.md).\n- Regenerated API references: [`docs/content/reference/sdk-reference/python/`](https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/tree/sdk-release/batch-42589989280/docs/content/reference/sdk-reference/python/), [`docs/content/reference/sdk-reference/typescript/`](https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/tree/sdk-release/batch-42589989280/docs/content/reference/sdk-reference/typescript/).\n\n## How this ships\n\n1. Release source is frozen at f22ab26848dbcc600131fb0b1d7261ab576ebb48. Later `next` commits and their changesets wait for the next release.\n2. Review the diff and approve this head. Approval must come from a writer other than the requester (@jkomyno). Do not push to this branch: the tag step only accepts the release bot's commit. To change the notes, fix the changesets on `next`, close this PR and request a new release.\n3. After approval and green checks, merge this PR. The release workflow rechecks the approval and tags this exact head `sdk-release/42589989280`; if the check fails, it creates no tag and asks you to revert this PR and request the release again.\n4. The tag run publishes the exact files the `SDK candidate` checks built and the `SDK candidate smoke` checks installed on this PR. If a publish job fails, use \"Re-run failed jobs\" on that run.\n5. After publishing, the bot opens a docs PR that pins the released npm versions, so twoslash checks the docs against them.\n\nRequest: https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/issues/5277\nPlanning run: https://github.com/ComposioHQ/composio/actions/runs/42589989280",
